title: Authorizations › Case page › Draft › Review, sign and what happens next
route: /authorizations/case/R-1042?tab=draft
intro: What happens when a person sends the request: the one 'Send to payer' in the header, its gate, the hand-off to New Case where a clinician signs, and where the request appears once it is sent.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the payer receiving the request is simulated. The summary signed in New Case is the one on this tab: edits, applied actions and added clinical context are all in it.
---
start s1 "Header 'Next:' block, on any tab"
decision dc "Do all four checks pass, and is the request still preparing?"
process off "'Send to payer' is greyed out\nits tooltip says why, e.g. 'Integrity 2/4: apply the matching actions'\nthe chip beside it counts the checks"
click sp "Click 'Send to payer'\n(the primary button once ready; tooltip: a clinician signs before anything is sent)"
click os "Click 'Open in review and sign' (header, always on)"
process rp "The case page finds this request's draft in New Case, or makes one from the request\nReview & submit when the request is ready, Authorization preparation when agents still have work"
goto gR "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Review & submit › Sign and send to payer"

group gSign "In New Case (drawn in its own diagram)"
  process sg "A licensed clinician signs\nThe UR coordinator cannot sign; Dr. Rivera can"
  ext py "Navigator sends the request through the payer's portal\n(demo: simulated)"
  doc pk "What goes out\nThe signed summary and the packet's documents"
endgroup

store rq "Dashboard: the request moves to 'Received'\nHistory: 'You signed as Dr. Rivera (clinician) and sent the request', 'Navigator sent the request through the payer's portal'"
screen cpg "Back on the case page or the Dashboard"
process qg "In Authorizations the row leaves In progress\nIt reads With the payer, marked 'New today' when the ledger did not have it\n'N sent today' counts it; the sidebar badge drops if it was due now or within 24 hours"
process cp "The case page of a sent request\nthe request's own status chip, e.g. 'Received'\n'Next: Wait for Beacon to decide' and a greyed-out 'Sent to payer'\nno Integrity chip"
goto gD "Continues in: Dashboard › Request drawer › Open and read a request"
goto gQ "Continues in: Authorizations › With the payer › A request sent today joins the list"

s1 --> dc
dc -->|No| off
dc -->|Yes| sp --> rp
s1 --> os --> rp
rp --> gR
gR --> sg --> py --> pk
sg --> rq --> cpg
cpg --> cp
cpg --> gD
rq --> qg --> gQ
